# [Domain] Continuity Brief

> **⚠️ RETIRED (v3.17) — do not use for new domains.** The hand-maintained
> continuity brief is superseded by the generated **orient** view: forward state
> lives in the thing graph (open-loop things + open conflicts) and is surfaced by
> `mdllm session-start`. This template is kept only so domains still carrying a
> legacy `continuity.md` validate during transition; its teardown is tracked. New
> domains create nothing here — see `session-memory.md` and
> `domain-specification-guide.md` → *The Orient View*.

This document bridges sessions. It is updated at the end of each session and loaded at the start of the next. It captures what is **still live** — not what was done (the commit stream, viewable via `mdllm worklog`), but what still needs to return.

Keep it short. If it grows past ~30 lines, stale items have accumulated.

